    heroImageAlt: "How Long Do Dental Implants Last? — dental implants patient education",
    bodyHtml: `
<p>Dental implants are designed to be a long-lasting tooth-replacement option, and many function well for many years. Their longevity depends on care, health and the restoration they support.</p><h2>What influences longevity</h2><p>The implant post itself is durable, while the crown or restoration may need maintenance or replacement over time. Gum health, bite forces, hygiene and habits such as smoking all affect how long an implant serves you.</p><h2>Making implants last</h2><p>Consistent home care, regular checkups and protecting against heavy grinding support implant longevity. Your clinician monitors the implant and surrounding tissues to catch any issues early.</p><h2>Working with an implant specialist in Vaughan</h2><p>Dr. Mehdi Adibrad is a trusted periodontal and implant specialist serving patients across Vaughan and the GTA. For those researching implant dentistry locally, the team at <a href="https://www.dfdentistry.ca/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener">Dr. Mehdi Adibrad's Vaughan practice</a> offers consultations for patients considering dental implants. A thorough consultation and examination are the clearest way to decide whether implants suit your situation.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do implants last forever?</h3><p>Implants are long-lasting but may not last indefinitely; care and health strongly influence outcomes.</p><h3>Does the crown last as long as the post?</h3><p>The restoration may need maintenance sooner than the integrated post, which tends to be very durable.</p><h3>What shortens implant lifespan?</h3><p>Gum inflammation, poor hygiene, smoking and heavy grinding can all reduce longevity.</p><p><em>This article is general educational information and is not a substitute for personalized advice from a licensed dental professional. Individual results vary, and treatment is determined following an examination.</em></p>
`,
